[ceiling] Purchased connector body/ear seat roof. This closed ceiling follows the complete body envelope with slip and the separate supported-face allowance. The ear bearing remains at depth 3.00, the body cavity at depth 4.15 and the insert anchor at depth 5.00. Tree(auto)/Default support reaches it from the empty contact opening before hardware installation. Printed cleanup, fit and retention are unqualified; accessible support alone does not establish removal effort.
alternatives: Sloping down into the source stadium consumes the purchased body clearance. A one-direction 45-degree rise over the 4.15 mm body depth consumes 4.15 of the current 6.75 mm to the crown, leaving 2.60 mm rather than the nominal 3 mm. A two-sided pitched relief could limit the rise to about 2.075 mm but would change the complete body-capture, insert-loading and adjoining lead-bore profiles; that alternative has not received an exact native or print review. Removing the roof opens the body seat through the retained crown.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
